{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitRecursion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitRecursion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanA4TightSlice","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.tight_slice_of_recursion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.tight_slice_of_recursion","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianDeficitRecursion.lean#L123-L136","doc":"**(CONDITIONAL on `BrunnianDeficitRecursion`.)  The exact-order tight slice for ALL A ≥ 3.**\nIf the deficit family obeys the strand-addition recursion, then at every `A ≥ 3` the deficit has\norder exactly `2(A−1)` with nonzero leading coefficient `(3/4)(−2)^{A−3}` — i.e. the ∀A\nnonvanishing content of `MilnorExactOrderConjecture` holds. Fully verified modulo the single\nopen class instance (§3b-cond conditional result). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.deficit_eq_closed_of_recursion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.deficit_eq_closed_of_recursion","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianDeficitRecursion.lean#L113-L121","doc":"Under the recursion, `D_{k+3}` equals the closed form `deficitClosed k` for every `k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.BrunnianDeficitRecursion.step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.BrunnianDeficitRecursion.step","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianDeficitRecursion.lean#L111-L111","doc":"Step: adding a strand multiplies the deficit by `−h²(h²+2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.BrunnianDeficitRecursion.base","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.BrunnianDeficitRecursion.base","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianDeficitRecursion.lean#L109-L109","doc":"Base: `D_3` is the proved A=3 closed-form deficit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.BrunnianDeficitRecursion.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.BrunnianDeficitRecursion.mk","kind":"ctor","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianDeficitRecursion.lean#L107-L107","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.BrunnianDeficitRecursion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.BrunnianDeficitRecursion","kind":"class","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianDeficitRecursion.lean#L102-L111","doc":"**(CONJECTURE — verified EXACT at A=3,4,5,6; structural TL derivation OPEN; NO instance.)**\nThe convention-D Brunnian deficit family `D : ℕ → ℝ → ℝ` obeys the strand-addition recursion,\nwith the proved A=3 deficit as base. Carrying this as an instance-less class is the honest open\nstate: four exact points are strong evidence, not a proof. The `-h²(h²+2)` factor is expected\nto come from the Temperley–Lieb / Jones–Wenzl strand-addition property. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.deficitClosed_tight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.deficitClosed_tight","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianDeficitRecursion.lean#L83-L100","doc":"**The closed form has the exact-order tight-slice property for every `k` (all A ≥ 3).**\n`D_k = h^{2(k+2)} · cofactor` with `cofactor 0 = (3/4)(−2)^k ≠ 0`. PROVED, unconditional in the\nclosed form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.deficitClosed_recursion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.deficitClosed_recursion","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianDeficitRecursion.lean#L72-L81","doc":"**The closed form satisfies the recursion** `D_{k+1} = −h²(h²+2)·D_k`. PROVED (ring). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.deficitClosed_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.deficitClosed_one","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianDeficitRecursion.lean#L65-L70","doc":"Base tie k=1: the closed form is exactly the proved A=4 deficit `1 − τ_4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.deficitClosed_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.deficitClosed_zero","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianDeficitRecursion.lean#L58-L63","doc":"Base tie k=0: the closed form is exactly the proved A=3 deficit `1 − τ_Borr`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.deficitClosed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.deficitClosed","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianDeficitRecursion.lean#L53-L56","doc":"The conjectured convention-D deficit closed form, indexed by `k = A − 3 ≥ 0`:\n`D_A(h) = (−1)^k · h^{2(k+2)} · (h²+2)^k · (h²+3)/(h²+4)` (A = k+3, so `2(k+2) = 2(A−1)`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}